<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>It is not a school or fact’ry</l><l>Or a chapel in the air;</l><l>But a garden where our Lord can plant and sow.</l><l>So He’s placed us all here corporately</l><l>To be His garden fair,</l><l>Where He’s free to cultivate and make us grow.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>Thus within the church-life garden</l><l>There’s a fruit-producing tree</l><l>Full of life and so available to eat.</l><l>So be simple, don’t be hardened,</l><l>Drop your concepts—eat that tree!</l><l>Take in Jesus every moment—He’s so sweet!</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>With the tree there is the water,</l><l>Flowing God in Christ to us,</l><l>Quenching all our dryness, ending all our strife.</l><l>Hallelujah! In His garden</l><l>Jesus flows Himself to us,</l><l>As the full supply for us to grow in life.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Aren’t you satisfied and thankful</l><l>That our Lord has brought you in</l><l>Where His pleasures and His riches flow so free?</l><l>So be happy and be joyful,</l><l>In the spirit feast on Him,</l><l>So God’s garden can bear fruit abundantly.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
